   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "War and hatte",
   "texto": [
    "For the past of «be / be» and «have», German uses almost always a simple form: **war** (era, was) and **hatte** (had).",
    "**Ich war zu Hause** (was at home), **Ich hatte keinen Hunger** (was not hungry).",
    "The forms of **ich** and **er** are equal, without termination."
   ]
